---
import Base from "@/layouts/Base.astro";
import Icon from "@/components/Icon.astro";
import { site, about } from "@/data/site";
import { withBase } from "@/lib/url";
---

<Base
  title="About Me"
  description="Learn more about Mitchell Salzman, ECE student at the University of Minnesota, medical device builder, and founder of STRIVE Medical."
>
  <div class="about-page">
    <!-- Hero banner -->
    <section class="about-hero">
      <div class="about-hero-inner">
        <div class="about-hero-text">
          <p class="eyebrow mb-4">About Me</p>
          <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold sm:text-5xl lg:text-6xl">
            Hi, I'm Mitchell.
          </h1>
          <p class="mt-4 max-w-lg text-lg leading-relaxed text-body">
            I build things that are useful to people, mostly in medical devices
            and health tech, where the stakes are real and the person on the
            other end of the design matters.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="about-hero-image">
          <!-- Replace src with your portrait photo -->
          <div class="portrait-placeholder"></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Main content -->
    <section class="about-body">
      <div class="about-grid">
        <!-- Left: images column -->
        <div class="about-images">
          <!-- Image 1: replace src with your photo -->
          <div class="about-img-slot about-img-slot--tall">
            <div class="img-placeholder">Photo 1</div>
          </div>
          <!-- Image 2: replace src with your photo -->
          <div class="about-img-slot">
            <div class="img-placeholder">Photo 2</div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Right: text column -->
        <div class="about-text">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-6">My Story</h2>

          <p class="text-body leading-relaxed mb-5">
            I study electrical and computer engineering at the University of
            Minnesota, on a combined bachelor's and master's track. That's the
            background, not really how I think about myself.
          </p>

          <p class="text-body leading-relaxed mb-5">
            What I care about most is building things that are useful to people.
            I like getting in early, when a problem is still messy, figuring out
            what's worth building, then helping make it real. That's the product
            side, and it's the part I love. Not just how something works, but why
            it exists, who it's for, and what makes them come back.
          </p>

          <p class="text-body leading-relaxed mb-5">
            The way I actually get there is systems thinking. I'm good at it,
            and I like it. Holding all the moving parts of a problem in view at
            once and seeing where they push and pull against each other. Project
            management is where that turns into something real for me, and I
            genuinely enjoy it: taking a messy pile of dependencies and shaping
            it into work a team can actually ship.
          </p>

          <!-- Image 3: inline break image -->
          <div class="about-img-slot about-img-inline mb-5">
            <div class="img-placeholder">Photo 3</div>
          </div>

          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-4">Why Medical Devices</h3>

          <p class="text-body leading-relaxed mb-5">
            Mostly I'm into medical devices and health tech. I like understanding
            how something is built, how it reaches the people who need it, and
            who it's really for, all at once, because in medical devices those
            three answers have to line up or the product never reaches anyone.
            Something technically impressive and clinically confused is still
            broken; it just takes longer for anyone to say so. What pulls me
            toward medical devices in particular is that the stakes are real.
            There's a person on the other end of the design, so the interesting
            question is rarely whether a thing <em>can</em> be done and almost
            always whether it <em>should</em> be, and for whom.
          </p>

          <p class="text-body leading-relaxed mb-5">
            Long term, I want to build products and eventually start my own
            company. Product management sits right where the technical, business,
            and people sides meet.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-4">STRIVE Medical</h3>

          <p class="text-body leading-relaxed mb-5">
            I started STRIVE Medical because I wanted to share the passion I have
            for the medical device industry, and because I wanted more people to
            feel confident in what they're actually capable of. At the end of the
            day, I want people to be able to walk into an interview and talk
            smart about the things they personally own and have contributed to,
            with the quiet confidence that only comes from having actually built
            the thing.
          </p>

          <p class="text-body leading-relaxed mb-5">
            What that looks like day to day is empowering my members: making them
            better public speakers, sharper researchers, prouder of what they
            build, and able to talk about it with real skill. When someone can
            speak with conviction about the thing they made, they stop feeling
            like they're along for the ride and start feeling like they're adding
            to what the whole group knows. A lot of it comes down to delegation,
            handing people real ownership and then pushing them a little further
            than they'd push themselves. But when you have people who actually
            care and want to get better, that push is usually all they need, and
            watching that development happen is the part I love most.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-4">Outside of Work</h3>

          <p class="text-body leading-relaxed mb-5">
            Weightlifting, motorcycling, snowmobiling and skiing, because a
            Minnesota winter may as well be good for something. Traveling around
            the world with my friends, trying to work on not overplanning. And
            camping, getting far enough out that the signal drops, and that's the
            point.
          </p>

          <!-- Quick facts -->
          <div class="facts-grid mt-8">
            <div class="fact-card">
              <span class="fact-label">Based in</span>
              <span class="fact-value">Minneapolis, MN</span>
            </div>
            <div class="fact-card">
              <span class="fact-label">Education</span>
              <span class="fact-value">BS + MS ECE, UMN</span>
            </div>
            <div class="fact-card">
              <span class="fact-label">Focus</span>
              <span class="fact-value">Medical devices & product</span>
            </div>
            <div class="fact-card">
              <span class="fact-label">Long term</span>
              <span class="fact-value">Build products, start a company</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Bottom image row -->
    <section class="about-bottom-images">
      <div class="bottom-images-grid">
        <!-- Image 4 -->
        <div class="about-img-slot">
          <div class="img-placeholder">Photo 4</div>
        </div>
        <!-- Image 5 -->
        <div class="about-img-slot">
          <div class="img-placeholder">Photo 5</div>
        </div>
        <!-- Image 6 -->
        <div class="about-img-slot">
          <div class="img-placeholder">Photo 6</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Back link -->
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-6 pb-24 sm:px-12 md:px-24 text-center">
      <a
        href={withBase("/")}
        class="link text-sm inline-flex items-center gap-2"
      >
        <Icon name="arrow" size={14} class="rotate-180" /> back to portfolio
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .about-page {
    --about-max: 1120px;
  }

  .about-hero {
    padding: 9rem 1.5rem 4rem;
    background: var(--color-surface-alt, #f8fafc);
  }

  .about-hero-inner {
    max-width: var(--about-max);
    margin: 0 auto;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 2.5rem;
    align-items: center;
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .about-hero-inner {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr auto;
    }
  }

  .about-hero-image .portrait-placeholder {
    width: 220px;
    height: 220px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #dce3ea 0%, #c4d0dc 100%);
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .about-hero-image .portrait-placeholder {
      width: 280px;
      height: 280px;
    }
  }

  .about-body {
    max-width: var(--about-max);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 4rem 1.5rem;
  }

  @media (min-width: 640px) {
    .about-body {
      padding: 4rem 3rem;
    }
  }

  .about-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 3rem;
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .about-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 2fr 3fr;
      gap: 3.5rem;
    }
  }

  .about-images {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .about-img-slot {
    border-radius: 12px;
    overflow: hidden;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-line, #e2e8f0);
  }

  .about-img-slot--tall .img-placeholder {
    height: 300px;
  }

  .about-img-inline {
    border-radius: 12px;
  }

  .img-placeholder {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #e2e8f0 0%, #cbd5e1 100%);
    height: 200px;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    color: #94a3b8;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .about-img-slot img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
  }

  .facts-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .fact-card {
    padding: 1rem;
    border-radius: 8px;
    background: var(--color-surface-alt, #f8fafc);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-line, #e2e8f0);
  }

  .fact-label {
    display: block;
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--color-muted, #94a3b8);
    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
  }

  .fact-value {
    display: block;
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-heading, #1e293b);
  }

  .about-bottom-images {
    max-width: var(--about-max);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 1.5rem 3rem;
  }

  @media (min-width: 640px) {
    .about-bottom-images {
      padding: 0 3rem 3rem;
    }
  }

  .bottom-images-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .bottom-images-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
